					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-227799#post-3709890</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-227799/that-goddamn-thing#post-3709890</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 14 Feb 2018 07:24:07 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>kodiakchris</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3623170</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Okay, I've read this three times now, and the discussion pages twice, and I'm still confused.</p> <p>Did Sorts shoot the toaster at the end (the door is mentioned as being opened, but no mention of them seeing the skip itself)? That's how I read it the first two times through through. But then we strangely have no mention of Schaffer after that.</p> <p>Also, &quot;The toaster hit the ground after two shots&#8230;&quot; sounds more like a human being shot.</p> <p>On the other hand, if Sorts finally lost the distinction between Schaffer and the toaster&#8230; and shot him&#8230; and didn't even realize it (thinking of the keycard as &quot;Schaffer's keycard&quot; at the same time, so wierd)&#8230; well, that seems to be the only way I can make sense of reading it.</p> <p>I just want to make sure other people are reading it the same way.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
